    "doc_text": "XIN_ENG_20061122.0228\n\nNEW DELHI, Nov. 22 , 2006 (Xinhua)\n\nUzbekistan pulls out of inaugural Asian Hopman Cup in India\n\n\n\n\nUzbekistan have withdrawn from the inaugural Asian Hopman Cup in India to focus on the 15th Asian Games, the organisers said on Wednesday.\n\nPhilippines have replaced Uzbekistan in the mixed team event starting on Thursday whose winners qualify for the Hopman Cup to be held in Perth, Australia from Dec. 30.\n\nHosts India, China and Japan have been drawn in Group A and Chinese Taipei, Thailand and Philippines in Group B.\n\nThe two group winners will meet in Sunday's final.\n\nIndian Davis Cup captain Leander Paes had already pulled out to recover from a finger injury before the Asian Games being held in Doha, Qatar from Dec. 1.",
